# Rule and conversion tool

A shop needs a deterministic discount tool using integer cents. Implement boundary cases and reject negative or non-integer amounts.

## Input and contract
input/fixture.json; input/dictionary.md; project version 1

## Finding and reproducible output
```json
[
  {
    "input": 0,
    "output": 0,
    "error": null
  },
  {
    "input": 9999,
    "output": 9999,
    "error": null
  },
  {
    "input": 10000,
    "output": 9000,
    "error": null
  },
  {
    "input": 10001,
    "output": 9001,
    "error": null
  },
  {
    "input": -1,
    "output": null,
    "error": "invalid_cents"
  },
  {
    "input": 10.5,
    "output": null,
    "error": "invalid_cents"
  },
  {
    "input": "10000",
    "output": null,
    "error": "invalid_cents"
  }
]
```

## Failure prevented
A negative amount is invalid rather than a valid discounted output.

## Decision and limits
Accept only the specified result set. Escalate a missing identity, permission, business probe or required not-run item. This is an original synthetic teaching reference, not evidence of learner execution or real employment.

## Contribution and handoff
Reference authored with AI assistance for Avemly. The learner must replace this attribution with their own factual contribution; review open criteria before archiving.

